## Rebuilding the paper

```
python scripts/make_tables.py --parquet results/{stable,shift,placebo}[_gp].parquet (all six) \
    --analysis results/{stable,shift,placebo}_analysis.json \
    --sensitivities results/sensitivities.json --out paper/tables --final
python scripts/make_figures.py --regimes stable shift placebo \
    --source stable=results/stable.parquet,results/stable_gp.parquet  (etc.) --out paper/figures
# compile in a scratchpad COPY, never in paper/:
latexmk -pdf -interaction=nonstopmode main.tex
```

- `make` is NOT installed; call `latexmk` directly. **Never pass
  `-halt-on-error=false`** — not a latexmk option; it aborts with "Bad options
  specified" and leaves a stale first-pass `main.log` whose float/overfull
  counts are phantom. That cost a wrong diagnosis once.
- TeX Live 2026 lives on **E:**, which has been unmounted twice. Fallback:
  `env -u ALL_PROXY <scratchpad>/tectonic/tectonic.exe -X compile --keep-logs main.tex`.
- **Delete any stale `paper/main.log` before trusting a build check** — an
  Aug-28 leftover was read as if current and reported phantom errors.
- Check `grep -c '^!' main.log` = 0, no "Float too large", no "Overfull",
  no "undefined".

## Rules that are easy to break

- Real-data runs need `allow_real=True` (the CLI passes it) — the auditable act.
- Never clip SVAR rates or Poisson means (addendum 3 §7): rejection only. The
  rejection FIRES on real data — a finding, recorded as method-failure rows.
- Losses are never imputed: `mortcal.inference` raises on non-finite input and
  on any attempt to rank conformal placeholder crps/logscore — conformal
  contrasts use `winkler95`. CBD (45 ages) never enters a ranking with
  100-age families.
- **Conformal cells have NO derived-quantity intervals** (e0/e65/ä65 → n/a).
  Their samples are uniform draws inside a band, an interval convention, not
  a predictive law. Computing coverage from them is meaningless — this fed a
  real defect once.
- Bootstrap p-values: B=4999, so a stored `0.0` supports only **p < 0.0002**.
  Never write "p < 0.0001".
- Population counts differ by regime AND family: shift 20 (GP 16), stable 18
  for the nine non-GP families (GP 16), placebo 11. Never write a blanket
  "twenty populations".
- **The multi-output GP needs 40 training years** (`min_years=40`) — the
  strictest floor in the study. It removes CHL, HKG, HRV, KOR from every GP
  cell in every regime. Documented in §4.
- Do not commit `results/parity/D_*.csv` / `E_*.csv` (raw HMD) or `Dataset/`.

## Lessons that cost real time

- **Never regex-edit LaTeX across float boundaries.** A regex meant to unwrap
  `\begin{table}...\end{table}` matched across two floats and deleted
  `tab-h4-age`, the entire H4 discussion and the PIT subsection heading —
  ~230 lines, no backup. A second regex attached four captions to the wrong
  function calls. Use anchored, exact-string edits.
- **GP worker memory is NOT stationary.** It grows across a population's 13
  origins and the 11 retained member fits of EnbPI/copula. An RSS reading
  taken minutes after launch understates the peak ~3×. Budget **~3.5 GB per
  GP worker**. JOBS=11 and JOBS=6 both OOM-killed on a 23 GB box; JOBS=4 was
  stable. Size GP passes off the peak, never the first measurement.
- **Size compute by available MEMORY, not cores.** The 24-core production box
  took 2 GP workers; the 12-core staging box took 4–6 and was faster.
- **Verifiers are not infallible.** Two adversarial findings were themselves
  wrong (a claimed tie in the 34/16 coverage split — there is none; and a
  claim that CBD is not the largest break contribution — it is, +0.102).
  Check each finding against the data before applying it.
- Heredocs mangle `\\` (backslash class in regexes collapses) — write helper
  scripts to files with the Write tool instead of piping heredocs.
- `pkill -f <pattern>` from an `ssh host "..."` one-liner matches the caller's
  own command line — use bracket patterns, or kill by process group.

## What remains

1. **111 pages is far beyond ASTIN Bulletin / AAS norms.** The five
   family × mechanism tables are page-spanning longtables (three regimes of
   column blocks ran 118pt past the text block, so regimes became ROWS). Most
   journals would want the bulk as supplementary material, leaving ~40 pages.
   Decide against the target journal's limits before submitting.
2. **The 99.5% longevity-tail quantile was never emitted** by the swept
   passes. `runner.py` now emits `{e0,e65,ann65}_q995`, and per-cell seeds
   reproduce samples bit-identically on the same device, so a re-score of
   shift+placebo would fill it. §5 and §8 both state plainly that no tail is
   reported. Both machines are now free if this is wanted.
3. Optional: `scripts/verify_quotes.py` re-checks every direct quote in the
   paper against `literature/txt/`. Re-run it after any prose edit.

